{"title":"2025 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the value of the following limit?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/0/400bd17e07c9a38cf59352b6305e9e2e69390711.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lim\\limits_{n \\to \\infty} \\left( \\dfrac{n-1}{n} \\right)^{n}\\]\" width=\"117\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/f/15f7b28a9c007217774c66a121a667bd8ab6f496.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0  \\quad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ 1  \\quad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ e  \\quad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{e}}  \\quad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\dfrac{1}{e}  \\quad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"323\" height=\"43\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/6/d06ba7a943d1b30dcd90d8354bab4b44a09e7ce7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{n-1}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"38\" /> is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/e/40eb4d4907fc8281e48f805a9519e3af010b06db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 - \\frac{1}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"38\" />. For any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2f9d612c42f0fc487d2ea822a0dfc77aa80c84.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lim\\limits_{n \\to \\infty} \\left(1 + \\frac{k}{n} \\right)^{n} = e^{k}\\]\" width=\"158\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>From this, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00fab47c0b9d0ce398d03e57d6720129d53434f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, the value of the limit is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/b/7bbbdeb127671ad640b41fcd63de66c131190dcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e^{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"17\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/3/e431a9e9ee4dcf70c906ec00936be7b944307835.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\dfrac{1}{e}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"59\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Calculus Contest\">2025 TMTA Calculus</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_17&a